        <body>
            <trans-unit id="9aed734">
                <source>description.book_route_book</source>
                <target>First segment of a book's url, e.g. "book" for /book/my-title. Left empty, the page is not served at all.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="35d55a2">
                <source>description.book_route_books</source>
                <target>First segment of the url listing the books, e.g. "books" for /books. The change applies straight away, but the former urls return a not-found page: set up a redirect if they are indexed. Left empty, the page is not served at all — which is what a site whose books are read under its own addresses sets here.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="2aef3b4">
                <source>description.book_route_serie</source>
                <target>First segment of a serie's url, e.g. "serie" for /serie/my-serie. Left empty, the page is not served at all.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="f349e22">
                <source>description.book_route_series</source>
                <target>First segment of the url listing the series, e.g. "series". Left empty, the page is not served at all.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="e0cab83">
                <source>description.book_route_strip</source>
                <target>First segment of a strip's url, e.g. "strip" for /strip/my-strip. Left empty, the page is not served at all.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="35eb84a">
                <source>description.book_route_strips</source>
                <target>First segment of the url listing the strips, e.g. "strips". Left empty, the page is not served at all.</target>
            </trans-unit>
